{{ includeTemplate "agents/authority.md" . }}
`Skill chains` and `guard-secrets` are Claude-specific written guards covered by that rule. An auto-mode classifier block is not a written rule, and is never worked around with variants either. When the blocked action was explicitly user-requested this turn, a subagent stops and reports, the main session reruns it identically once, and on a second block stops and surfaces the classifier's reason.
When spawning a Claude subagent for a task that includes a user-requested state-changing command, quote the user's request verbatim in the delegation prompt so the classifier receives that authorization in its user-message slot.

